{
  "case_id": "2016-16-327",
  "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Jae Lee accepted a plea based on his counsel's assurance he would not be deported. Counsel had it exactly backward. The plea resulted in mandatory banishment from the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: In -- in State courts, do State -- are State courts mandated to follow what we do in the Federal courts under Rule 11; that is to say, before the guilty plea is accepted, to advise the defendant of all of his rights? I'm sure they are."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument this morning in case 16-327, Lee v. United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay. A conviction on this charge then could result in your being deported."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: We often get people who come in and say I wasn't told about a plea, and I would have pled guilty. And judges then look at the facts and find out that the defendant was claiming he was innocent, despite overwhelming evidence that he or she was guilty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: All right. But -- but -- let's -- the question -- but the question that was -- was -- was put to you with reference to Strickland was in the context of what might happen at a trial with different evidence, with different arguments."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court Record",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF ERIC J. FEIGIN ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric J. Feigin (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nThe crux of a Padilla claim is the defendant's contention that if he had constitutionally competent counsel, that counsel could have given him a legitimate chance at avoiding a removal with particular -- avoiding a conviction with particular removal consequences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: -- in the plea negotiation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What's the windfall?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What is the answer to the lesser-included offense? Was that -- is that out of the picture?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can the INS still proceed to deport this person? Does it need a conviction given -- given his admission at -- at the earlier plea?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. BURSCH)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, I don't want to lose the point that Justice Sotomayor raised, that this isn't just keep this plea or go to trial. There's also the opportunity to negotiate other plea alternatives. And we give a couple of those in our reply brief, including one where there was a defendant with two-and-a-half kilograms of meth who was able to get a plea conviction with lessened deportation consequences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-327",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5e78e30aa07fbf83b86897d3deeb6597d3c20ed1b067a704a77d01dcfde0a5f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5e78e30aa07-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Case is submitted."
    },
